  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — differences from the reference value (2400 Euros), their probabilities, and a comparison of expected deviations — is partially present in the individual’s reasoning. The individual considers the +100 Euro gain (difference above reference) with 33% probability and the -2400 Euro loss (difference below reference) with 1% probability, which aligns with the inputs required by the decision reason. Furthermore, the justification weighs the favorable upside against the small risk, which reflects an evaluation of the mean difference implicitly. Although the individual does not explicitly compute expected differences, the reasoning pattern — evaluating gains and losses relative to the sure outcome and integrating their probabilities — closely matches the rule of the decision reason. The focus on the relative attractiveness of a small risk for a chance at a better outcome, anchored to the sure amount, supports the use of this reason. Therefore, it is highly likely the individual used this decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
}

